      {
       "label": "local short form",
       "text": "Aruba"
      },
      {
       "label": "etymology",
       "text": "the origin of the island's name is unclear; according to tradition, the name comes from the Spanish phrase <em>oro hubo</em> (\"there was gold\"), but no gold was ever found on the island; other possible sources are either the local word <em>oruba</em> (\"well-situated\") or a combination of two Carib Indian words, <em>ora </em>and <em>oubao</em> (\"shell\" and \"island,\" respectively)"
      }
     ]
